{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"debug":1},true],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"zotero":1,"inscriptions":7,"isBulletin":155},{"title":2,"author":3,"date":4,"citation":5,"uri":6},"Sulla dedica bilingue del Priapo bifronte di Aci-Catania","Ribezzo","1925","\u003Cspan>F. Ribezzo, «Sulla dedica bilingue del Priapo bifronte di Aci-Catania», \u003Ci>Rivista Indo-Greco-Italica di filologia - lingua - antichità\u003C/i> 9, fasc. 1–2 (1925): 65–66\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/7UG9RHJL",[8],{"file":9,"uri":9,"title":10,"status":11,"editions":13,"editionAuthor":38,"type":39,"objectType":43,"material":47,"condition":54,"layoutDesc":55,"handNote":62,"date":76,"places":80,"geo":90,"country":85,"provenance":82,"provenanceGeo":94,"region":97,"settlement":87,"repository":98,"textLang":99,"tmNumber":15,"facsimile":107,"letterHeights":114,"publications":117,"zotero":127,"keywords":137,"html":146,"bibl":147,"bulletinDateSort":152,"citedRangeSort":153,"languageSort":154,"materialSort":48,"typeSort":40},"ISic002753","Fragment of a bilingual dedication to Priapus",{"_":12},"draft",[14,17,20,22,25,28,30,32,34,36],{"_":15,"type":16},"175851","TM",{"_":18,"type":19},"072907","EDR",{"type":21},"EDH",{"_":23,"type":24},"16201127","EDCS",{"_":26,"type":27},"329566","PHI",{"_":29,"type":27},"329567",{"_":31,"type":27},"329622",{"_":33,"type":27},"329623",{"_":35,"type":27},"331217",{"_":37,"type":27},"332862",null,{"_":40,"ana":41,"ref":42},"dedication","#function.dedication","https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Dedication",{"_":44,"ana":45,"ref":46},"plaque","#object.plaque","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259.html",{"_":48,"ana":49,"type":50,"subtype":51,"ref":53},"marble","#material.inorganic.stone","stone.unspecified",[52],"unverified","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html","",{"layout":56},{"_":57,"rs":58,"damage":54},"Five lines of regularly spaced Greek letters followed by three lines of Latin letters. The first two lines of Latin text follow the same spacing as the Greek text; the final line is seemingly centered, more widely spaced (with interpuncts) and separated by a slightly greater interval from the lines above. Although the top of the stone is damaged, the visible space above line 1 is greater than that between the following lines.\n                                    \n                                \t\n\t\t\t",{"_":59,"ana":60,"ref":61},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":63,"dimensions":64},"Regular, well-cut Greek letters with clearly defined serifs at the end of strokes: Omicron, omega and theta all have rhomboid form; in some instances this is actually a pentagonal form, flat across the top; Omega is open at the bottom; Sigma is four bar and regular; Epsilon has equal horizontal strokes; Alpha has broken bar; the diagonal of the Nu starts and finishes well below/above the ends of the vertical strokes. The Latin letters show the beginnings of the move towards cursive forms: M has extended upper strokes and the midpoint reaches to the bottom of the line; A also has extended upper stroke and lacks a cross-bar; O is rounded, in contrast to the Greek text, as is Q with extended tail; P is open; R is closed; E has short upward slanting strokes; L has a long foot, forming almost a C.",[65,72],{"type":66,"l":67,"from":68,"to":69,"h":70,"unit":71,"atLeast":70,"atMost":70},"letterHeight","Lines 1-8","line1","line8","20","mm",{"type":73,"l":74,"from":68,"to":75,"unit":71},"interlinear","Interlineation\n                                ","line2",{"_":77,"notBefore":78,"notAfter":79},"Late 2nd — 4th century CE",180,400,[81,86],{"_":82,"type":83,"ref":84,"region":85},"Acium","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462067","Sicilia",{"_":87,"type":88,"ref":89,"region":85},"Aci San Antonio","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2525383",[91],[92,93],37.57533,15.17411,[95,96],37.598818,15.126647,"Sicily","unknown",{"_":100,"mainLang":101,"otherLangs":102,"ana":103,"languages":104},"Ancient Greek and Latin","grc","la","#bilingualism.biversion.complementary",[105,106],"Ancient Greek","Latin",{"n":108,"url":109,"height":110,"width":111,"desc":112,"surfaceType":113},"screen","ISic002753_tiled.tif","2790px","3431px","Scan of photo in NSA 1922 p.494 fig.2","front",[115],{"atLeast":116,"atMost":116},20,[118,119,119,119,119,120,121,122,123,120,124,125,126],"L'année épigraphique: revue des publications épigraphiques relatives a l'antiquité romaine., 1888-","Supplementum epigraphicum graecum, 1923-","Manganaro, 1988, La Sicilia da Sesto Pompeo a Diocleziano","Manganaro, 1994, Iscrizioni, epigrafi ed epigrammi in Greco della Sicilia orientale di epoca romana","Notizie degli scavi di antichità, 1876-","Manganaro, 1977, Per la storia dei culti nella Sicilia greca","Sabbadini, 1923, Priapo bifronte","Ribezzo, 1925, Sulla dedica bilingue del Priapo bifronte di Aci-Catania","Wick, 1926, Due nuovi saturnii?",[128,129,129,129,129,130,131,132,133,130,134,135,136],"R46KDTZX","F2GG87EQ","RZSFKACR","532NF7SV","4MCP2PVV","JQHZXXJN","PURER8C4","7UG9RHJL","SP2B89MW",[138,139,140,40,44,48,141,142,143,144,142,145,101],"isic002753","fragment of a bilingual dedication to priapus",{"_":12},"acium","aci san antonio","sicilia","sicily","ancient greek and latin","\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"aba\">section a\u003C/span>  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"diva--interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"aa-l1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]κεν ἔνθα καὶ ἔνθ̣[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"aa-l2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]σθαι τοὺς ἀπʼἄστεω[ς\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"aa-l3-interpretive\">\u003C